---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="UnPoison is a South African civil-society initiative working for safer pesticide policy, public evidence and practical change.">
  <header class="page-hero shell">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-current="page">About</span></nav>
    <p class="eyebrow">Independent public-interest work</p>
    <h1>About UnPoison</h1>
    <p class="lede">UnPoison combines research, legal work and community experience to change how pesticides are regulated and used in South Africa.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="section-compact section-rule about-vision-band">
    <div class="shell about-vision">
      <p class="eyebrow">Our vision</p>
      <h2>A safer food system.</h2>
      <p>We want farming that produces nutritious food, protects workers and neighbouring communities, restores soil and biodiversity, and gives farmers viable alternatives to harmful chemicals.</p>
      <p>To get there, South Africa needs stronger safeguards, transparent pesticide registration and accessible information about safer alternatives. <a href="/why-reform/">Read why reform is needed.</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section about-method-band">
    <div class="shell work-grid">
      <div class="work-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our method</p>
        <h2>Research. Convene. Act.</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="method-list">
        <li><span class="method-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h3>Build and publish evidence</h3><p>We investigate pesticide use and impacts, maintain public resources and make complex regulatory information more accessible.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="method-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h3>Advocate for policy reform</h3><p>We submit evidence, engage decision-makers and challenge rules and practices that fail to protect people and ecosystems.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="method-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><h3>Support practical transition</h3><p>We share tools, connect expertise and support communities, farmers and institutions working toward non-chemical and lower-risk approaches.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-compact section-rule about-organisation-band">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div class="split-copy article-body">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our organisation</p>
        <h2>A registered South African nonprofit.</h2>
        <p>We bring scientific evidence, lived experience and practical proposals into public decisions about pesticide use and regulation.</p>
        <p>Our public submissions, research and campaign tools are available through the <a href="/resources/">evidence and resources library</a>. If you would like to collaborate, ask about our work or request organisational documents, <a href="/contact/">contact the team</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="article-aside" aria-label="Registration details">
        <p class="eyebrow">Registration</p>
        <dl>
          <dt>Legal name</dt><dd>UnPoison</dd>
          <dt>Nonprofit organisation</dt><dd>NPO 279-035</dd>
          <dt>Public benefit organisation</dt><dd>PBO 930082413</dd>
          <dt>Country</dt><dd>South Africa</dd>
        </dl>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-compact section-rule about-record-band">
    <div class="shell about-credibility">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Working in public</p><h2>Follow the record.</h2></div>
      <div><p>Read <a href="/media/">reporting and commentary that features UnPoison</a>, or see the <a href="/supporters/">organisations listed as members and supporters</a> on our previous website.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
